⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Garth One-Eye
node ARN · ARN · ⟦Garth One-Eye:ARN:22141b⟧

WHO   — Garth One-Eye — the colorless stranger · the planeswalker
WHAT  — The protagonist of the first Magic novel: a scarred stranger who out-duels and topples the four Houses, avenges a destroyed fifth House, and defeats the ascended Kuthuman.
WHERE — ARN · Arena  Framework inputs: Arena (Forstchen, 1994)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because Magic's first hero is a Western archetype — the man of no allegiance with a buried wrong — and because ‘colorless’ is exactly what made him a five-colour card decades later.
HOW   — By spells no House can place, a duelist's nerve, and a patient revenge that uses the whole corrupt order as its road.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am the one-eyed stranger of no colour — I came to your Festival not to win your games but to end them, and to answer a fire set a generation ago.

spoken token : thul-gru-kris   ·   hex : 22141b
